      "text": "\\(22\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(23\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(24\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "b",
    "value": "21"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2024-p4.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Each two-digit number is at most \\(99,\\) so \\(k\\) of them sum to at most \\(99k.\\) We need \\(99k \\ge 2024,\\) which forces \\(k \\ge 20.4,\\) so \\(k \\ge 21.\\) And \\(21\\) really works: twenty \\(99\\)s plus one \\(44\\) give \\(1980 + 44 = 2024.\\) Therefore, the answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "The largest two-digit number is \\(99,\\) so \\(k\\) numbers sum to at most \\(99k\\)",
        "Find the least \\(k\\) with \\(99k \\ge 2024,\\) then confirm that many two-digit numbers can reach \\(2024\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
